{"id":"mahabharata-13-017","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · The names of Shiva","summary":{"en":"Krishna tells how the sage Upamanyu began to recite the collected names of Shiva, first purifying himself with folded hands, and gives the long hymn of Shiva's thousand names. He ends by saying that the pure one who recites it with restraint for a year gains the fruit of a horse sacrifice.","kn":"ಉಪಮನ್ಯು ಶುದ್ಧನಾಗಿ ಕೈ ಜೋಡಿಸಿ ಶಿವನ ಹೆಸರುಗಳ ಸಂಗ್ರಹ ಪಠಿಸಲು ಆರಂಭಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ಹೇಳಿ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಶಿವನ ಸಹಸ್ರನಾಮ ಸ್ತೋತ್ರ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶುದ್ಧನಾಗಿ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಚಾರಿಯಾಗಿ ಜಿತೇಂದ್ರಿಯನಾಗಿ ಒಂದು ವರ್ಷ ಪಠಿಸುವವನಿಗೆ ಅಶ್ವಮೇಧ ಫಲ.","hi":"कृष्ण बताते हैं कि उपमन्यु ने पवित्र होकर हाथ जोड़कर शिव के नामों का संग्रह पढ़ना आरम्भ किया, और वे शिव के सहस्र नामों का लम्बा स्तोत्र देते हैं। जो शुद्ध, संयमी और जितेन्द्रिय होकर एक वर्ष इसका पाठ करे उसे अश्वमेध का फल मिलता है।","te":"ఉపమన్యుడు శుద్ధుడై చేతులు జోడించి శివ నామ సంగ్రహం పఠించడం ప్రారంభించిన తీరు చెప్పి కృష్ణుడు శివ సహస్ర నామ స్తోత్రం ఇస్తాడు. శుద్ధుడై, బ్రహ్మచారిగా, జితేంద్రియుడై ఏడాది పఠించేవాడికి అశ్వమేధ ఫలం.","ta":"உபமன்யு தூய்மையுடன் கை கூப்பி சிவனின் பெயர்களின் தொகுப்பை ஓதத் தொடங்கியதைக் கூறி, சிவனின் ஆயிரம் நாமங்களைக் கொண்ட நீண்ட துதியைக் கிருஷ்ணன் தருகிறார். தூய்மையாய் புலனடக்கி ஓராண்டு ஓதுபவன் அசுவமேத பலன் பெறுவான்.","ml":"കൂപ്പുകൈയോടെ സ്വയം ശുദ്ധമാക്കിയശേഷം ഉപമന്യു ശിവന്റെ നാമങ്ങളുടെ സമാഹാരം ജപിച്ചുതുടങ്ങിയതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു; ആയിരം നാമങ്ങളുള്ള ശിവസ്തോത്രം അദ്ദേഹം നൽകുന്നു. ഒരു വർഷം നിയന്ത്രണത്തോടെ ഇത് ജപിക്കുന്ന ശുദ്ധന് അശ്വമേധയാഗത്തിന്റെ ഫലം ലഭിക്കുമെന്ന് പറഞ്ഞ് അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः स प्रयतो भूत्वा मम तात युधिष्ठिर ।\nप्राञ्जलिः प्राह विप्रर्षिर्नामसंहारमादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, dear Yudhishthira, that sage-brahmin, purified and with joined palms, began to recite the collection of names from the start."}},{"text":"उपमन्युरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Upamanyu said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"ब्रह्मप्रोक्तैरृषिप्रोक्तैर्वेदवेदाङ्गसंभवैः ।\nसर्वलोकेषु विख्यातैः स्थाणुं स्तोष्यामि नामभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will praise Sthanu with names declared by Brahma and by sages, born of the Vedas and Vedangas, and famed in all the worlds."}},{"n":3,"text":"महद्भिर्विहितैः सत्यैः सिद्धैः सर्वार्थसाधकैः ।\nऋषिणा तण्डिना भक्त्या कृतैर्देवकृतात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are true names, set forth by great beings, effective for every purpose, made with devotion by the sage Tandi, whose soul was shaped by the God."}},{"n":4,"text":"यथोक्तैर्लोकविख्यातैर्मुनिभिस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः ।\nप्रवरं प्रथमं स्वर्ग्यं सर्वभूतहितं शुभम् ।\nश्रुतैः सर्वत्र जगति ब्रह्मलोकावतारितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are as stated by the renowned seers who perceive the truth: foremost, first, leading to heaven, good for all beings, auspicious, heard everywhere in the world after being brought down from Brahma's world."}},{"n":5,"text":"यत्तद्रहस्यं परमं ब्रह्मप्रोक्तं सनातनम् ।\nवक्ष्ये यदुकुलश्रेष्ठ शृणुष्वावहितो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"That supreme, eternal secret spoken by Brahma I will tell you, best of the Yadu line; listen to me attentively."}},{"n":6,"text":"परत्वेन भवं देवं भक्तस्त्वं परमेश्वरम् ।\nतेन ते श्रावयिष्यामि यत्तद्ब्रह्म सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are a devotee who regards Bhava as the supreme God and Lord; therefore I will let you hear that eternal Brahman."}},{"n":7,"text":"न शक्यं विस्तरात्कृत्स्नं वक्तुं शर्वस्य केनचित् ।\nयुक्तेनापि विभूतीनामपि वर्षशतैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one, even with discipline, could describe in full all of Sharva's manifestations in detail, even in hundreds of years."}},{"n":8,"text":"यस्यादिर्मध्यमन्तश्च सुरैरपि न गम्यते ।\nकस्तस्य शक्नुयाद्वक्तुं गुणान्कार्त्स्न्येन माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His beginning, middle and end are unknown even to the gods; who could describe his qualities completely, Madhava?"}},{"n":9,"text":"किं तु देवस्य महतः संक्षिप्तार्थपदाक्षरम् ।\nशक्तितश्चरितं वक्ष्ये प्रसादात्तस्य चैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet, by his grace and as far as I am able, I will tell of the great God's deeds in a condensed form of words and syllables."}},{"n":10,"text":"अप्राप्येह ततोऽनुज्ञां न शक्यः स्तोतुमीश्वरः ।\nयदा तेनाभ्यनुज्ञातः स्तुवत्येव सदा भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without his leave one cannot praise the Lord here; only when he permits does one praise Bhava at all."}},{"n":11,"text":"अनादिनिधनस्याहं सर्वयोनेर्महात्मनः ।\nनाम्नां कंचित्समुद्देशं वक्ष्ये ह्यव्यक्तयोनिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of him who has no beginning or end, the great-souled source of all, whose own source is unmanifest, I will give only a small part of his names."}},{"n":12,"text":"वरदस्य वरेण्यस्य विश्वरूपस्य धीमतः ।\nशृणु नामसमुद्देशं यदुक्तं पद्मयोनिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear the summary of the names of the boon-giving, most choice, many-formed and wise one, as spoken by the Lotus-born."}},{"n":13,"text":"दश नामसहस्राणि यान्याह प्रपितामहः ।\nतानि निर्मथ्य मनसा दध्नो घृतमिवोद्धृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ten thousand names the great-grandsire spoke have been churned by the mind, as butter is drawn out of curd."}},{"n":14,"text":"गिरेः सारं यथा हेम पुष्पात्सारं यथा मधु ।\nघृतात्सारं यथा मण्डस्तथैतत्सारमुद्धृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As gold is the essence of a mountain, honey of a flower, and cream of ghee, so this is the essence drawn out of them."}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वपाप्मापहमिदं चतुर्वेदसमन्वितम् ।\nप्रयत्नेनाधिगन्तव्यं धार्यं च प्रयतात्मना ।\nशान्तिकं पौष्टिकं चैव रक्षोघ्नं पावनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It removes all sin and goes with the four Vedas; it should be studied with effort and held by one of controlled mind. It brings peace and prosperity, destroys demons, and is greatly purifying."}},{"n":16,"text":"इदं भक्ताय दातव्यं श्रद्दधानास्तिकाय च ।\nनाश्रद्दधानरूपाय नास्तिकायाजितात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"It should be given to a devotee, to a believing person, and to one who is not a doubter; not to one who lacks faith, a nonbeliever, or one who has not mastered himself."}},{"n":17,"text":"यश्चाभ्यसूयते देवं भूतात्मानं पिनाकिनम् ।\nस कृष्ण नरकं याति सह पूर्वैः सहानुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, whoever resents the God, the self of beings, the wielder of Pinaka, goes to hell with his forefathers and his followers."}},{"n":18,"text":"इदं ध्यानमिदं योगमिदं ध्येयमनुत्तमम् ।\nइदं जप्यमिदं ज्ञानं रहस्यमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nइदं ज्ञात्वान्तकालेऽपि गच्छेद्धि परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is meditation, this is yoga, this is the unsurpassed object of meditation; this is to be chanted, this is knowledge, this is the highest secret. Knowing it, one may reach the supreme goal even at the hour of death."}},{"n":19,"text":"पवित्रं मङ्गलं पुण्यं कल्याणमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nनिगदिष्ये महाबाहो स्तवानामुत्तमं स्तवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed one, I will recite this holy, auspicious, meritorious, blessed hymn, the best of hymns."}},{"n":20,"text":"इदं ब्रह्मा पुरा कृत्वा सर्वलोकपितामहः ।\nसर्वस्तवानां दिव्यानां राजत्वे समकल्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma, grandfather of all worlds, composed this long ago and made it the king of all divine hymns."}},{"n":21,"text":"तदाप्रभृति चैवायमीश्वरस्य महात्मनः ।\nस्तवराजेति विख्यातो जगत्यमरपूजितः ।\nब्रह्मलोकादयं चैव स्तवराजोऽवतारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From then on it has been known as the king of hymns of the great-souled Lord, honored by the gods in the world; and this king of hymns was brought down from Brahma's world."}},{"n":22,"text":"यस्मात्तण्डिः पुरा प्राह तेन तण्डिकृतोऽभवत् ।\nस्वर्गाच्चैवात्र भूलोकं तण्डिना ह्यवतारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because Tandi declared it in the past, it came to be called Tandi's work; and by Tandi it was brought here to the earth from heaven."}},{"n":23,"text":"सर्वमङ्गलमङ्गल्यं सर्वपापप्रणाशनम् ।\nनिगदिष्ये महाबाहो स्तवानामुत्तमं स्तवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed one, I will recite this best of hymns, the blessing of all blessings and destroyer of all sins."}},{"n":24,"text":"ब्रह्मणामपि यद्ब्रह्म पराणामपि यत्परम् ।\nतेजसामपि यत्तेजस्तपसामपि यत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is the Brahman among Brahmans, the supreme among the supreme, the radiance among radiances, the austerity among austerities."}},{"n":25,"text":"शान्तीनामपि या शान्तिर्द्युतीनामपि या द्युतिः ।\nदान्तानामपि यो दान्तो धीमतामपि या च धीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is the peace among peaces, the splendor among splendors, the self-controlled among the self-controlled, the wisdom among the wise."}},{"n":26,"text":"देवानामपि यो देवो मुनीनामपि यो मुनिः ।\nयज्ञानामपि यो यज्ञः शिवानामपि यः शिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the God among gods, the sage among sages, the sacrifice among sacrifices, the auspicious among the auspicious."}},{"n":27,"text":"रुद्राणामपि यो रुद्रः प्रभुः प्रभवतामपि ।\nयोगिनामपि यो योगी कारणानां च कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the Rudra among Rudras, the lord among lords, the yogi among yogis, the cause of causes."}},{"n":28,"text":"यतो लोकाः संभवन्ति न भवन्ति यतः पुनः ।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतस्य हरस्यामिततेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the Hara of boundless radiance, the self of all beings, from whom the worlds arise and into whom they go again."}},{"n":29,"text":"अष्टोत्तरसहस्रं तु नाम्नां शर्वस्य मे शृणु ।\nयच्छ्रुत्वा मनुजश्रेष्ठ सर्वान्कामानवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear the one thousand and eight names of Sharva, best of men; hearing them you will obtain all your desires."}},{"n":30,"text":"स्थिरः स्थाणुः प्रभुर्भानुः प्रवरो वरदो वरः ।\nसर्वात्मा सर्वविख्यातः सर्वः सर्वकरो भवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sthira (steady), Sthanu (the firm one), Prabhu (lord), Bhanu (sun), Pravara (excellent), Varada (boon-giver), Vara (the choice), Sarvatma (self of all), Sarvavikhyata (known to all), Sarva (the all), Sarvakara (maker of all), Bhava (the being)."}},{"n":31,"text":"जटी चर्मी शिखण्डी च सर्वाङ्गः सर्वभावनः ।\nहरिश्च हरिणाक्षश्च सर्वभूतहरः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jati (matted-haired), Charmi (wearing hide), Shikhandi (crested), Sarvanga (all-limbed), Sarvabhavana (cause of all things), Hari, Harinaksha (deer-eyed), Sarvabhutahara (taker of all beings), Prabhu."}},{"n":32,"text":"प्रवृत्तिश्च निवृत्तिश्च नियतः शाश्वतो ध्रुवः ।\nश्मशानचारी भगवान्खचरो गोचरोऽर्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pravritti (activity), Nivritti (rest), Niyata (restrained), Shashvata (eternal), Dhruva (fixed), Shmashanachari (haunter of cremation grounds), Bhagavan, Khachara (sky-goer), Gochara (earth-goer), Ardana (afflicter)."}},{"n":33,"text":"अभिवाद्यो महाकर्मा तपस्वी भूतभावनः ।\nउन्मत्तवेशप्रच्छन्नः सर्वलोकप्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhivadya (worthy of salutation), Mahakarma (of great deeds), Tapasvi (ascetic), Bhutabhavana (maker of beings), Unmattaveshapracchanna (hidden in the guise of a madman), Sarvalokaprajapati (lord of creatures of all worlds)."}},{"n":34,"text":"महारूपो महाकायः सर्वरूपो महायशाः ।\nमहात्मा सर्वभूतश्च विरूपो वामनो मनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maharupa (of great form), Mahakaya (huge-bodied), Sarvarupa (of every form), Mahayasha (greatly famed), Mahatma (great soul), Sarvabhuta (all beings), Virupa (misshapen), Vamana (dwarf), Manu."}},{"n":35,"text":"लोकपालोऽन्तर्हितात्मा प्रसादो हयगर्दभिः ।\nपवित्रश्च महांश्चैव नियमो नियमाश्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lokapala (guardian of worlds), Antarhitatma (self hidden within), Prasada (grace), Hayagardabhi (who has horse and ass), Pavitra (pure), Mahan (great), Niyama (rule), Niyamashraya (support of rules)."}},{"n":36,"text":"सर्वकर्मा स्वयंभूश्च आदिरादिकरो निधिः ।\nसहस्राक्षो विरूपाक्षः सोमो नक्षत्रसाधकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvakarma (of all actions), Svayambhu (self-born), Adi (the first), Adikara (maker of beginnings), Nidhi (treasure), Sahasraksha (thousand-eyed), Virupaksha (of strange eyes), Soma, Nakshatrasadhaka (who governs the stars)."}},{"n":37,"text":"चन्द्रसूर्यगतिः केतुर्ग्रहो ग्रहपतिर्वरः ।\nअद्रिरद्र्यालयः कर्ता मृगबाणार्पणोऽनघः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chandrasuryagati (course of moon and sun), Ketu, Graha (planet), Grahapati (lord of planets), Vara, Adri (mountain), Adryalaya (mountain-dweller), Karta (doer), Mrigabanarpana (who aimed an arrow at the deer), Anagha (sinless)."}},{"n":38,"text":"महातपा घोरतपा अदीनो दीनसाधकः ।\nसंवत्सरकरो मन्त्रः प्रमाणं परमं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahatapa (of great austerity), Ghoratapa (of fierce austerity), Adina (not wretched), Dinasadhaka (helper of the wretched), Samvatsarakara (maker of the year), Mantra, Pramana (authority), Paramam Tapa (supreme austerity)."}},{"n":39,"text":"योगी योज्यो महाबीजो महारेता महातपाः ।\nसुवर्णरेताः सर्वज्ञः सुबीजो वृषवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yogi, Yojya (to be joined), Mahabija (great seed), Maharetas (of great seed), Mahatapa, Suvarnaretas (golden-seeded), Sarvajna (all-knowing), Subija (of good seed), Vrishavahana (bull-rider)."}},{"n":40,"text":"दशबाहुस्त्वनिमिषो नीलकण्ठ उमापतिः ।\nविश्वरूपः स्वयंश्रेष्ठो बलवीरो बलो गणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dashabahu (ten-armed), Animisha (unwinking), Nilakantha (blue-throated), Umapati (lord of Uma), Vishvarupa (all-formed), Svayamshreshtha (best by himself), Balavira (hero of strength), Bala (strength), Gana (host)."}},{"n":41,"text":"गणकर्ता गणपतिर्दिग्वासाः काम्य एव च ।\nपवित्रं परमं मन्त्रः सर्वभावकरो हरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ganakarta (maker of hosts), Ganapati (lord of hosts), Digvasa (clad in the directions), Kamya (desirable), Pavitram Paramam Mantra (the pure, supreme mantra), Sarvabhavakara (maker of all states), Hara."}},{"n":42,"text":"कमण्डलुधरो धन्वी बाणहस्तः कपालवान् ।\nअशनी शतघ्नी खड्गी पट्टिशी चायुधी महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kamandaludhara (bearing a water pot), Dhanvi (archer), Banahasta (arrow in hand), Kapalavan (bearing a skull), Ashani (with thunderbolt), Shataghni (with the hundred-slayer weapon), Khadgi (swordsman), Pattishi (with a spear), Ayudhi (armed), Mahan."}},{"n":43,"text":"स्रुवहस्तः सुरूपश्च तेजस्तेजस्करो निधिः ।\nउष्णीषी च सुवक्त्रश्च उदग्रो विनतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sruvahasta (ladle in hand), Surupa (beautiful), Tejas (radiance), Tejaskara (maker of radiance), Nidhi, Ushnishi (turbaned), Suvaktra (fair-faced), Udagra (lofty), Vinata (bowed)."}},{"n":44,"text":"दीर्घश्च हरिकेशश्च सुतीर्थः कृष्ण एव च ।\nसृगालरूपः सर्वार्थो मुण्डः कुण्डी कमण्डलुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dirgha (tall), Harikesha (tawny-haired), Sutirtha (a good ford), Krishna (dark), Srigalarupa (jackal-formed), Sarvartha (all purposes), Munda (shaven), Kundi (with a vessel), Kamandalu."}},{"n":45,"text":"अजश्च मृगरूपश्च गन्धधारी कपर्द्यपि ।\nऊर्ध्वरेता ऊर्ध्वलिङ्ग ऊर्ध्वशायी नभस्तलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aja (unborn), Mrigarupa (deer-formed), Gandhadhari (bearer of fragrance), Kapardi (with matted locks), Urdhvareta (of upward seed), Urdhvalinga (with upright sign), Urdhvashayi (lying upward), Nabhastala (sky-plane)."}},{"n":46,"text":"त्रिजटश्चीरवासाश्च रुद्रः सेनापतिर्विभुः ।\nअहश्चरोऽथ नक्तं च तिग्ममन्युः सुवर्चसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trijata (three-braided), Chiravasa (wearing bark), Rudra, Senapati (army chief), Vibhu (all-pervading), Aharchara (who goes by day), Naktam (night), Tigmamanyu (of sharp wrath), Suvarchasa (of fine splendor)."}},{"n":47,"text":"गजहा दैत्यहा लोको लोकधाता गुणाकरः ।\nसिंहशार्दूलरूपश्च आर्द्रचर्माम्बरावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gajaha (elephant-slayer), Daityaha (demon-slayer), Loka (world), Lokadhata (world-supporter), Gunakara (mine of virtues), Simhashardularupa (lion and tiger form), Ardracharmambaravrita (clad in a wet hide)."}},{"n":48,"text":"कालयोगी महानादः सर्ववासश्चतुष्पथः ।\nनिशाचरः प्रेतचारी भूतचारी महेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kalayogi (yogi of Time), Mahanada (of great roar), Sarvavasa (dwelling in all), Chatushpatha (crossroads), Nishachara (night-walker), Pretachari (walker among ghosts), Bhutachari (walker among spirits), Maheshvara (great lord)."}},{"n":49,"text":"बहुभूतो बहुधनः सर्वाधारोऽमितो गतिः ।\nनृत्यप्रियो नित्यनर्तो नर्तकः सर्वलासकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahubhuta (many beings), Bahudhana (much wealth), Sarvadhara (support of all), Amita (limitless), Gati (goal), Nrityapriya (fond of dancing), Nityanarta (ever-dancing), Nartaka (dancer), Sarvalasaka (all-playing)."}},{"n":50,"text":"घोरो महातपाः पाशो नित्यो गिरिचरो नभः ।\nसहस्रहस्तो विजयो व्यवसायो ह्यनिन्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghora (terrible), Mahatapa, Pasha (noose), Nitya (eternal), Girichara (mountain-roamer), Nabha (sky), Sahasrahasta (thousand-handed), Vijaya (victory), Vyavasaya (resolve), Anindita (blameless)."}},{"n":51,"text":"अमर्षणो मर्षणात्मा यज्ञहा कामनाशनः ।\nदक्षयज्ञापहारी च सुसहो मध्यमस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Amarshana (unforgiving), Marshanatma (forgiving soul), Yajnaha (destroyer of sacrifice), Kamanashana (destroyer of desire), Dakshayajnapahari (taker of Daksha's sacrifice), Susaha (very patient), Madhyama (middle)."}},{"n":52,"text":"तेजोपहारी बलहा मुदितोऽर्थो जितो वरः ।\nगम्भीरघोषो गम्भीरो गम्भीरबलवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tejopahari (remover of splendor), Balaha (slayer of strength), Mudita (joyful), Artha (meaning), Jita (conquered), Vara, Gambhiraghosha (deep-voiced), Gambhira (deep), Gambhirabalavahana (of deep might and mount)."}},{"n":53,"text":"न्यग्रोधरूपो न्यग्रोधो वृक्षकर्णस्थितिर्विभुः ।\nतीक्ष्णतापश्च हर्यश्वः सहायः कर्मकालवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nyagrodharupa (banyan-formed), Nyagrodha (banyan), Vrikshakarnasthiti (abiding in the tree's ear), Vibhu, Tikshnatapa (of sharp heat), Haryashva (with tawny horses), Sahaya (helper), Karmakalavit (knower of the time for action)."}},{"n":54,"text":"विष्णुप्रसादितो यज्ञः समुद्रो वडवामुखः ।\nहुताशनसहायश्च प्रशान्तात्मा हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishnuprasadita (propitiated by Vishnu), Yajna (sacrifice), Samudra (ocean), Vadavamukha (the mare-faced fire), Hutashanasahaya (companion of fire), Prashantatma (tranquil soul), Hutashana (fire)."}},{"n":55,"text":"उग्रतेजा महातेजा जयो विजयकालवित् ।\nज्योतिषामयनं सिद्धिः संधिर्विग्रह एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ugratejas (of fierce power), Mahatejas (of great power), Jaya (victory), Vijayakalavit (knower of the time of victory), Jyotishamayana (course of the lights), Siddhi (success), Sandhi (union), Vigraha (form)."}},{"n":56,"text":"शिखी दण्डी जटी ज्वाली मूर्तिजो मूर्धगो बली ।\nवैणवी पणवी ताली कालः कालकटंकटः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhi (crested), Dandi (staff-bearer), Jati, Jvali (flaming), Murtija (born of form), Murdhaga (head-dwelling), Bali (mighty), Vainavi (flute player), Panavi (drummer), Tali (cymbal player), Kala (time), Kalakatankata (devourer of Time)."}},{"n":57,"text":"नक्षत्रविग्रहविधिर्गुणवृद्धिर्लयोऽगमः ।\nप्रजापतिर्दिशाबाहुर्विभागः सर्वतोमुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakshatravigrahavidhi (arranger of the stars' forms), Gunavriddhi (increase of qualities), Laya (dissolution), Agama (not to be approached), Prajapati, Dishabahu (arms the directions), Vibhaga (division), Sarvatomukha (facing all sides)."}},{"n":58,"text":"विमोचनः सुरगणो हिरण्यकवचोद्भवः ।\nमेढ्रजो बलचारी च महाचारी स्तुतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vimochana (liberator), Suragana (host of gods), Hiranyakavachodbhava (born in a golden armor), Medhraja (born of seed), Balachari (roaming in strength), Mahachari (great roamer), Stuta (praised)."}},{"n":59,"text":"सर्वतूर्यनिनादी च सर्ववाद्यपरिग्रहः ।\nव्यालरूपो बिलावासी हेममाली तरंगवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvaturyaninadi (sounding all instruments), Sarvavadyaparigraha (accepting all music), Vyalarupa (serpent-formed), Bilavasi (dwelling in caves), Hemamali (golden-garlanded), Tarangavit (knower of waves)."}},{"n":60,"text":"त्रिदशस्त्रिकालधृक्कर्मसर्वबन्धविमोचनः ।\nबन्धनस्त्वसुरेन्द्राणां युधि शत्रुविनाशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tridasha (the thirty-gods), Trikaladhrik (upholder of the three times), Karmasarvabandhavimochana (freer from all bonds of action), Bandhana (binder), Asurendranam Yudhi Shatruvinashana (binder of the demon lords, destroyer of foes in battle)."}},{"n":61,"text":"सांख्यप्रसादो दुर्वासाः सर्वसाधुनिषेवितः ।\nप्रस्कन्दनो विभागश्च अतुल्यो यज्ञभागवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sankhyaprasada (favor of Sankhya), Durvasa (the hard-clad), Sarvasadhunishevita (served by all good men), Praskandana (leaping forth), Vibhaga, Atulya (peerless), Yajnabhagavit (knower of sacrificial shares)."}},{"n":62,"text":"सर्वावासः सर्वचारी दुर्वासा वासवोऽमरः ।\nहेमो हेमकरो यज्ञः सर्वधारी धरोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvavasa (dwelling in all), Sarvachari (moving everywhere), Durvasa, Vasava (like Indra), Amara (immortal), Hema (gold), Hemakara (gold-maker), Yajna, Sarvadhari (holder of all), Dharottama (best supporter)."}},{"n":63,"text":"लोहिताक्षो महाक्षश्च विजयाक्षो विशारदः ।\nसंग्रहो निग्रहः कर्ता सर्पचीरनिवासनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lohitaksha (red-eyed), Mahaksha (great-eyed), Vijayaksha (victorious-eyed), Visharada (skilled), Sangraha (collector), Nigraha (restrainer), Karta, Sarpachiranivasana (clad in snake-skin)."}},{"n":64,"text":"मुख्योऽमुख्यश्च देहश्च देहर्द्धिः सर्वकामदः ।\nसर्वकालप्रसादश्च सुबलो बलरूपधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mukhya (chief), Amukhya (without chief), Deha (body), Dehardhi (prosperity of the body), Sarvakamada (giver of all desires), Sarvakalaprasada (gracious at all times), Subala (very strong), Balarupadhrik (bearing forms of strength)."}},{"n":65,"text":"आकाशनिधिरूपश्च निपाती उरगः खगः ।\nरौद्ररूपोंऽशुरादित्यो वसुरश्मिः सुवर्चसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Akashanidhirupa (treasure and form of the sky), Nipati (who falls), Uraga (serpent), Khaga (bird), Raudrarupa (terrible form), Amshu (ray), Aditya (sun), Vasurashmi (rays of wealth), Suvarchasi (splendid)."}},{"n":66,"text":"वसुवेगो महावेगो मनोवेगो निशाचरः ।\nसर्वावासी श्रियावासी उपदेशकरो हरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasuvega (swift as Vasus), Mahavega (of great speed), Manovega (swift as mind), Nishachara, Sarvavasi (dweller in all), Shriyavasi (dwelling in prosperity), Upadeshakara (giver of teaching), Hara."}},{"n":67,"text":"मुनिरात्मपतिर्लोके संभोज्यश्च सहस्रदः ।\nपक्षी च पक्षिरूपी च अतिदीप्तो विशां पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Muni (sage), Atmapati (lord of selves), Sambhojya (to be feasted), Sahasrada (giver of thousands), Pakshi (bird), Pakshirupi (bird-formed), Atidipta (very bright), Vishampati (lord of peoples)."}},{"n":68,"text":"उन्मादो मदनाकारो अर्थार्थकररोमशः ।\nवामदेवश्च वामश्च प्राग्दक्षिण्यश्च वामनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unmada (madness), Madanakara (form of love), Arthakara (maker of wealth), Romasha (hairy), Vamadeva, Vama (left), Pragdakshinya (kind from the front), Vamana."}},{"n":69,"text":"सिद्धयोगापहारी च सिद्धः सर्वार्थसाधकः ।\nभिक्षुश्च भिक्षुरूपश्च विषाणी मृदुरव्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Siddhayogapahari (remover of the yoga of perfected ones), Siddha (perfected), Sarvarthasadhaka (accomplisher of all aims), Bhikshu (mendicant), Bhikshurupa (in mendicant form), Vishani (horned), Mridu (gentle), Avyaya (imperishable)."}},{"n":70,"text":"महासेनो विशाखश्च षष्टिभागो गवां पतिः ।\nवज्रहस्तश्च विष्कम्भी चमूस्तम्भन एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahasena (great army), Vishakha (Skanda), Shashtibhaga (sixty portions), Gavam Pati (lord of cows), Vajrahasta (thunderbolt in hand), Vishkambhi (prop), Chamustambhana (stopper of armies)."}},{"n":71,"text":"ऋतुरृतुकरः कालो मधुर्मधुकरोऽचलः ।\nवानस्पत्यो वाजसेनो नित्यमाश्रमपूजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ritu (season), Ritukara (maker of seasons), Kala, Madhu (spring), Madhukara (bee), Achala (unmoving), Vanaspatya (of trees), Vajasena (of the strong army), Nityamashramapujita (ever honored in hermitages)."}},{"n":72,"text":"ब्रह्मचारी लोकचारी सर्वचारी सुचारवित् ।\nईशान ईश्वरः कालो निशाचारी पिनाकधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmachari (celibate student), Lokachari (moving in the worlds), Sarvachari, Sucharavit (knower of good conduct), Ishana (ruler), Ishvara (lord), Kala, Nishachari, Pinakadhrik (bearer of Pinaka)."}},{"n":73,"text":"नन्दीश्वरश्च नन्दी च नन्दनो नन्दिवर्धनः ।\nभगस्याक्षिनिहन्ता च कालो ब्रह्मविदां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nandishvara (lord of Nandi), Nandi, Nandana (delighter), Nandivardhana (increaser of Nandi), Bhagasyakshinihanta (blinder of Bhaga's eye), Kala, Brahmavidam Vara (best of Brahman-knowers)."}},{"n":74,"text":"चतुर्मुखो महालिङ्गश्चारुलिङ्गस्तथैव च ।\nलिङ्गाध्यक्षः सुराध्यक्षो लोकाध्यक्षो युगावहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chaturmukha (four-faced), Mahalinga (great sign), Charulinga (beautiful sign), Lingadhyaksha (overseer of the linga), Suradhyaksha (overseer of the gods), Lokadhyaksha (overseer of the world), Yugavaha (bearer of the ages)."}},{"n":75,"text":"बीजाध्यक्षो बीजकर्ता अध्यात्मानुगतो बलः ।\nइतिहासकरः कल्पो गौतमोऽथ जलेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bijadhyaksha (overseer of seed), Bijakarta (maker of seed), Adhyatmanuga (follower of the inner self), Bala, Itihasakara (maker of history), Kalpa (age), Gautama, Jaleshvara (lord of waters)."}},{"n":76,"text":"दम्भो ह्यदम्भो वैदम्भो वश्यो वश्यकरः कविः ।\nलोककर्ता पशुपतिर्महाकर्ता महौषधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dambha (pretense), Adambha (without pretense), Vaidambha (beyond pretense), Vashya (obedient), Vashyakara (subduer), Kavi (seer), Lokakarta (maker of the world), Pashupati (lord of beasts), Mahakarta (great doer), Mahaushadhi (great herb)."}},{"n":77,"text":"अक्षरं परमं ब्रह्म बलवाञ्शक्र एव च ।\nनीतिर्ह्यनीतिः शुद्धात्मा शुद्धो मान्यो मनोगतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Akshara (the imperishable), Parama Brahma (supreme Brahman), Balavan (strong), Shakra (Indra), Niti (policy), Aniti (beyond policy), Shuddhatma (pure soul), Shuddha (pure), Manya (honored), Manogati (course of the mind)."}},{"n":78,"text":"बहुप्रसादः स्वपनो दर्पणोऽथ त्वमित्रजित् ।\nवेदकारः सूत्रकारो विद्वान्समरमर्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahuprasada (very gracious), Svapana (sleep), Darpana (mirror), Tvamitrajit (conqueror of enemies), Vedakara (maker of the Vedas), Sutrakara (maker of aphorisms), Vidvan (learned), Samaramardana (crusher in battle)."}},{"n":79,"text":"महामेघनिवासी च महाघोरो वशीकरः ।\nअग्निज्वालो महाज्वालो अतिधूम्रो हुतो हविः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahameghanivasi (dweller in great clouds), Mahaghora (very terrible), Vashikara (subduer), Agnijvala (flame of fire), Mahajvala (great flame), Atidhumra (very smoky), Huta (offered), Havi (oblation)."}},{"n":80,"text":"वृषणः शंकरो नित्यो वर्चस्वी धूमकेतनः ।\nनीलस्तथाङ्गलुब्धश्च शोभनो निरवग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishana (potent), Shankara (bringer of welfare), Nitya (eternal), Varchasvi (radiant), Dhumaketana (smoke-bannered), Nila (blue), Angalubdha (attached to the limbs), Shobhana (beautiful), Niravagraha (unrestrained)."}},{"n":81,"text":"स्वस्तिदः स्वस्तिभावश्च भागी भागकरो लघुः ।\nउत्सङ्गश्च महाङ्गश्च महागर्भः परो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Svastida (giver of well-being), Svastibhava (nature of well-being), Bhagi (sharer), Bhagakara (maker of shares), Laghu (light), Utsanga (lap), Mahanga (great-limbed), Mahagarbha (great womb), Para (supreme), Yuva (youth)."}},{"n":82,"text":"कृष्णवर्णः सुवर्णश्च इन्द्रियः सर्वदेहिनाम् ।\nमहापादो महाहस्तो महाकायो महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishnavarna (dark-hued), Suvarna (golden), Indriya (sense) of all embodied beings, Mahapada (great-footed), Mahahasta (great-handed), Mahakaya (great-bodied), Mahayasha (greatly famed)."}},{"n":83,"text":"महामूर्धा महामात्रो महानेत्रो दिगालयः ।\nमहादन्तो महाकर्णो महामेढ्रो महाहनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahamurdha (great-headed), Mahamatra (of great measure), Mahanetra (great-eyed), Digalaya (home of the directions), Mahadanta (great-toothed), Mahakarna (great-eared), Mahamedhra (great-membered), Mahahanu (great-jawed)."}},{"n":84,"text":"महानासो महाकम्बुर्महाग्रीवः श्मशानधृक् ।\nमहावक्षा महोरस्को अन्तरात्मा मृगालयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahanasa (great-nosed), Mahakambu (great-necked, shell-like), Mahagriva (great-necked), Shmashanadhrik (bearer of cremation grounds), Mahavaksha (broad-chested), Mahoraska (great-chested), Antaratma (inner self), Mrigalaya (home of deer)."}},{"n":85,"text":"लम्बनो लम्बितोष्ठश्च महामायः पयोनिधिः ।\nमहादन्तो महादंष्ट्रो महाजिह्वो महामुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lambana (hanging), Lambitoshtha (hanging-lipped), Mahamaya (of great illusion), Payonidhi (ocean), Mahadanta, Mahadamshtra (great-tusked), Mahajihva (great-tongued), Mahamukha (great-mouthed)."}},{"n":86,"text":"महानखो महारोमा महाकेशो महाजटः ।\nअसपत्नः प्रसादश्च प्रत्ययो गिरिसाधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahanakha (great-nailed), Maharoma (great-haired), Mahakesha (great-maned), Mahajata (greatly matted), Asapatna (rivalless), Prasada (grace), Pratyaya (trust), Girisadhana (mountain-resort)."}},{"n":87,"text":"स्नेहनोऽस्नेहनश्चैव अजितश्च महामुनिः ।\nवृक्षाकारो वृक्षकेतुरनलो वायुवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Snehana (affectionate), Asnehana (unattached), Ajita (unconquered), Mahamuni (great sage), Vrikshakara (tree-formed), Vrikshaketu (tree-bannered), Anala (fire), Vayuvahana (wind-borne)."}},{"n":88,"text":"मण्डली मेरुधामा च देवदानवदर्पहा ।\nअथर्वशीर्षः सामास्य ऋक्सहस्रामितेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mandali (circled), Merudhama (dwelling on Meru), Devadanavadarpaha (crusher of the pride of gods and demons), Atharvashira (whose head is the Atharva Veda), Sama (Sama Veda) is his, Riksahasramitekshana (of thousand Rik-verse eyes)."}},{"n":89,"text":"यजुःपादभुजो गुह्यः प्रकाशो जङ्गमस्तथा ।\nअमोघार्थः प्रसादश्च अभिगम्यः सुदर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yajuhpadabhuja (whose feet and arms are the Yajus), Guhya (secret), Prakasha (light), Jangama (moving), Amoghartha (of unfailing purpose), Prasada, Abhigamya (approachable), Sudarshana (fair to see)."}},{"n":90,"text":"उपहारप्रियः शर्वः कनकः काञ्चनः स्थिरः ।\nनाभिर्नन्दिकरो भाव्यः पुष्करस्थपतिः स्थिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Upaharapriya (fond of offerings), Sharva, Kanaka (gold), Kanchana (golden), Sthira, Nabhi (navel), Nandikara (maker of joy), Bhavya (to be), Pushkarasthapati (lord of the lotus place), Sthira."}},{"n":91,"text":"द्वादशस्त्रासनश्चाद्यो यज्ञो यज्ञसमाहितः ।\nनक्तं कलिश्च कालश्च मकरः कालपूजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dvadashatrasana (terrifier of the twelve), Adya (primal), Yajna, Yajnasamahita (absorbed in sacrifice), Naktam (night), Kali (strife), Kala, Makara (crocodile), Kalapujita (worshipped by Time)."}},{"n":92,"text":"सगणो गणकारश्च भूतभावनसारथिः ।\nभस्मशायी भस्मगोप्ता भस्मभूतस्तरुर्गणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sagana (with hosts), Ganakara (maker of hosts), Bhutabhavanasarathi (charioteer of beings' origin), Bhasmashayi (lying in ashes), Bhasmagopta (guardian of ashes), Bhasmabhuta (ash-become), Taru (tree), Gana."}},{"n":93,"text":"अगणश्चैव लोपश्च महात्मा सर्वपूजितः ।\nशङ्कुस्त्रिशङ्कुः संपन्नः शुचिर्भूतनिषेवितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agana (without host), Lopa (disappearance), Mahatma, Sarvapujita (honored by all), Shanku (peg), Trishanku (three-pegged), Sampanna (accomplished), Shuchi (pure), Bhutanishevita (served by beings)."}},{"n":94,"text":"आश्रमस्थः कपोतस्थो विश्वकर्मा पतिर्वरः ।\nशाखो विशाखस्ताम्रोष्ठो ह्यम्बुजालः सुनिश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashramastha (in the hermitage), Kapotastha (on the dove), Vishvakarma (builder of all), Pati (lord), Vara, Shakha (branch), Vishakha, Tamroshtha (copper-lipped), Ambujala (water-netted), Sunishchaya (of firm resolve)."}},{"n":95,"text":"कपिलोऽकपिलः शूर आयुश्चैव परोऽपरः ।\nगन्धर्वो ह्यदितिस्तार्क्ष्यः सुविज्ञेयः सुसारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kapila (tawny), Akapila (not tawny), Shura (hero), Ayu (life), Para (higher), Apara (lower), Gandharva, Aditi, Tarkshya (Garuda), Suvijneya (easily known), Susarathi (good charioteer)."}},{"n":96,"text":"परश्वधायुधो देव अर्थकारी सुबान्धवः ।\nतुम्बवीणी महाकोप ऊर्ध्वरेता जलेशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Parashvadhayudha (axe-armed), Deva, Arthakari (accomplisher of aims), Subandhava (good kinsman), Tumbavini (lute-player), Mahakopa (greatly wrathful), Urdhvareta, Jaleshaya (lying in the waters)."}},{"n":97,"text":"उग्रो वंशकरो वंशो वंशनादो ह्यनिन्दितः ।\nसर्वाङ्गरूपो मायावी सुहृदो ह्यनिलोऽनलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ugra (fierce), Vamshakara (founder of lineages), Vamsha (lineage), Vamshanada (flute sound), Anindita, Sarvangarupa (of every limb's form), Mayavi (illusionist), Suhrid (friend), Anila (wind), Anala (fire)."}},{"n":98,"text":"बन्धनो बन्धकर्ता च सुबन्धनविमोचनः ।\nस यज्ञारिः स कामारिर्महादंष्ट्रो महायुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bandhana (binder), Bandhakarta (maker of bonds), Subandhanavimochana (loosener of fine bonds), Sa Yajnari (foe of sacrifice, i.e., Daksha's), Sa Kamari (foe of Desire), Mahadamshtra, Mahayudha (of great weapons)."}},{"n":99,"text":"बाहुस्त्वनिन्दितः शर्वः शंकरः शंकरोऽधनः ।\nअमरेशो महादेवो विश्वदेवः सुरारिहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahu (arm), Anindita, Sharva, Shankara, Shankara, Adhana (without wealth), Amaresha (lord of immortals), Mahadeva (great god), Vishvadeva (god of all), Suraribaha (slayer of the gods' foes)."}},{"n":100,"text":"अहिर्बुध्नो निरृतिश्च चेकितानो हरिस्तथा ।\nअजैकपाच्च कापाली त्रिशङ्कुरजितः शिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ahirbudhnya, Nirriti, Chekitana, Hari, Ajaikapat, Kapali (skull-bearer), Trishanku, Ajita, Shiva."}},{"n":101,"text":"धन्वन्तरिर्धूमकेतुः स्कन्दो वैश्रवणस्तथा ।\nधाता शक्रश्च विष्णुश्च मित्रस्त्वष्टा ध्रुवो धरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhanvantari, Dhumaketu, Skanda, Vaishravana (Kubera), Dhata, Shakra, Vishnu, Mitra, Tvashta, Dhruva, Dhara."}},{"n":102,"text":"प्रभावः सर्वगो वायुरर्यमा सविता रविः ।\nउदग्रश्च विधाता च मान्धाता भूतभावनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prabhava (origin), Sarvaga (going everywhere), Vayu (wind), Aryaman, Savita, Ravi, Udagra (lofty), Vidhata, Mandhata, Bhutabhavana."}},{"n":103,"text":"रतितीर्थश्च वाग्मी च सर्वकामगुणावहः ।\nपद्मगर्भो महागर्भश्चन्द्रवक्त्रो मनोरमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ratitirtha (ford of love), Vagmi (eloquent), Sarvakamagunavaha (bringer of all desired qualities), Padmagarbha (lotus-womb), Mahagarbha, Chandravaktra (moon-faced), Manorama (delighting the mind)."}},{"n":104,"text":"बलवांश्चोपशान्तश्च पुराणः पुण्यचञ्चुरी ।\nकुरुकर्ता कालरूपी कुरुभूतो महेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Balavan (strong), Upashanta (calm), Purana (ancient), Punyachanchuri (famed for merit), Kurukarta (maker of the Kurus), Kalarupi (in Time's form), Kurubhuta (Kuru-become), Maheshvara."}},{"n":105,"text":"सर्वाशयो दर्भशायी सर्वेषां प्राणिनां पतिः ।\nदेवदेवमुखोऽसक्तः सदसत्सर्वरत्नवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvashaya (abiding in all), Darbhashayi (lying on darbha grass), Sarveshaam Pranin Pati (lord of all living beings), Devadevamukha (face of the god of gods), Asakta (unattached), Sadasat (being and non-being), Sarvaratnavit (knower of all jewels)."}},{"n":106,"text":"कैलासशिखरावासी हिमवद्गिरिसंश्रयः ।\nकूलहारी कूलकर्ता बहुविद्यो बहुप्रदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kailasashikharavasi (dweller on Kailasa's peak), Himavadgirisamshraya (resting on the Himalaya), Kulahari (carrier off of banks), Kulakarta (maker of banks), Bahuvidya (many-sciences), Bahuprada (giver of much)."}},{"n":107,"text":"वणिजो वर्धनो वृक्षो नकुलश्चन्दनश्छदः ।\nसारग्रीवो महाजत्रुरलोलश्च महौषधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vanija (merchant), Vardhana (increaser), Vriksha (tree), Nakula (mongoose), Chandana (sandalwood), Chhada (covering), Saragriva (strong-necked), Mahajatru (great collar-bone), Alola (steady), Mahaushadha (great herb)."}},{"n":108,"text":"सिद्धार्थकारी सिद्धार्थश्छन्दोव्याकरणोत्तरः ।\nसिंहनादः सिंहदंष्ट्रः सिंहगः सिंहवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Siddharthakari (accomplisher of aims), Siddhartha (whose aims are met), Chhandovyakaranottara (beyond metre and grammar), Simhanada (lion-roar), Simhadamshtra (lion-fanged), Simhaga (lion-going), Simhavahana (lion-mounted)."}},{"n":109,"text":"प्रभावात्मा जगत्कालस्तालो लोकहितस्तरुः ।\nसारङ्गो नवचक्राङ्गः केतुमाली सभावनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prabhavatma (self of power), Jagatkala (Time of the world), Tala (palm), Lokahita (benefit of the world), Taru (tree), Sharanga (bow), Navachakranga (with nine-wheeled limbs), Ketumali (wearing banners), Sabhavana."}},{"n":110,"text":"भूतालयो भूतपतिरहोरात्रमनिन्दितः ।\nवाहिता सर्वभूतानां निलयश्च विभुर्भवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhutalaya (home of beings), Bhutapati (lord of beings), Aho-ratra (day and night), Anindita, Vahita (carrier) of all beings, Nilaya (abode), Vibhu, Bhava."}},{"n":111,"text":"अमोघः संयतो ह्यश्वो भोजनः प्राणधारणः ।\nधृतिमान्मतिमान्दक्षः सत्कृतश्च युगाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Amogha (unfailing), Samyata (restrained), Ashva (horse), Bhojana (food), Pranadharana (sustainer of life), Dhritiman (steady), Matiman (wise), Daksha (skilled), Satkrita (honored), Yugadhipa (lord of ages)."}},{"n":112,"text":"गोपालिर्गोपतिर्ग्रामो गोचर्मवसनो हरः ।\nहिरण्यबाहुश्च तथा गुहापालः प्रवेशिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gopali (herdsman), Gopati (lord of cattle), Grama (village), Gocharmavasana (clad in cowhide), Hara, Hiranyabahu (golden-armed), Guhapala (guardian of caves) of those who enter."}},{"n":113,"text":"प्रतिष्ठायी महाहर्षो जितकामो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nगन्धारश्च सुरालश्च तपःकर्मरतिर्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pratishthayi (firm-standing), Mahaharsha (great joy), Jitakama (conqueror of desire), Jitendriya (conqueror of senses), Gandhara (the note Gandhara), Surala (the note), Tapahkarmarati (delighting in austerity), Dhanu (bow)."}},{"n":114,"text":"महागीतो महानृत्तो ह्यप्सरोगणसेवितः ।\nमहाकेतुर्धनुर्धातुर्नैकसानुचरश्चलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahagita (great song), Mahanritta (great dance), Apsarogana-sevita (served by hosts of Apsaras), Mahaketu (great banner), Dhanurdhata (bow-bearer), Naikasanuchara (with many peak companions), Chala (moving)."}},{"n":115,"text":"आवेदनीय आवेशः सर्वगन्धसुखावहः ।\nतोरणस्तारणो वायुः परिधावति चैकतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Avedaniya (not to be conveyed), Avesha (possession), Sarvagandhasukhavaha (bringer of the pleasure of all fragrances), Torana (gateway), Tarana (rescuer), Vayu, Paridhavati Chaikata (running about alone)."}},{"n":116,"text":"संयोगो वर्धनो वृद्धो महावृद्धो गणाधिपः ।\nनित्य आत्मसहायश्च देवासुरपतिः पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Samyoga (union), Vardhana (increase), Vriddha (old), Mahavriddha (very old), Ganadhipa (lord of hosts), Nitya (eternal), Atmasahaya (self-helped), Devasurapati (lord of gods and demons), Pati."}},{"n":117,"text":"युक्तश्च युक्तबाहुश्च द्विविधश्च सुपर्वणः ।\nआषाढश्च सुषाढश्च ध्रुवो हरिहणो हरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yukta (joined), Yuktabahu (arms joined), Dvividha (twofold), Suparvana (of fine joints), Ashadha, Sushadha, Dhruva, Harihana (slayer of Hari), Hara."}},{"n":118,"text":"वपुरावर्तमानेभ्यो वसुश्रेष्ठो महापथः ।\nशिरोहारी विमर्षश्च सर्वलक्षणभूषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vapu (body), Avartamanebhyo Vasu (wealth for those who turn to him), Vasushreshtha (best of Vasus), Mahapatha (great path), Shirohari (head-taker), Vimarsha (reflection), Sarvalakshanabhushita (adorned with all marks)."}},{"n":119,"text":"अक्षश्च रथयोगी च सर्वयोगी महाबलः ।\nसमाम्नायोऽसमाम्नायस्तीर्थदेवो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aksha (axle), Rathayogi (joined to the chariot), Sarvayogi (yogi of all), Mahabala (greatly strong), Samamnaya (tradition), Asamamnaya (beyond tradition), Tirthadeva (god of fords), Maharatha (great chariot warrior)."}},{"n":120,"text":"निर्जीवो जीवनो मन्त्रः शुभाक्षो बहुकर्कशः ।\nरत्नप्रभूतो रक्ताङ्गो महार्णवनिपानवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nirjiva (lifeless), Jivana (life), Mantra, Shubhaksha (fair-eyed), Bahukarkasha (very rough), Ratnaprabhuta (rich in jewels), Raktanga (red-limbed), Mahamavanipanavit (knower of the great ocean's drinking)."}},{"n":121,"text":"मूलो विशालो ह्यमृतो व्यक्ताव्यक्तस्तपोनिधिः ।\nआरोहणो निरोहश्च शैलहारी महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mula (root), Vishala (vast), Amrita (immortal), Vyaktavyakta (manifest and unmanifest), Taponidhi (treasury of austerity), Arohana (ascent), Niroha (descent), Shailahari (taker of mountains), Mahatapa."}},{"n":122,"text":"सेनाकल्पो महाकल्पो युगायुगकरो हरिः ।\nयुगरूपो महारूपः पवनो गहनो नगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Senakalpa (army-order), Mahakalpa (great age), Yugayugakara (maker of age after age), Hari, Yugarupa (form of the ages), Maharupa (great form), Pavana (wind), Gahana (impenetrable), Naga (mountain)."}},{"n":123,"text":"न्यायनिर्वापणः पादः पण्डितो ह्यचलोपमः ।\nबहुमालो महामालः सुमालो बहुलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nyayanirvapana (fulfiller of justice), Pada (foot), Pandita (scholar), Achalopama (like an immovable mountain), Bahumala (many garlands), Mahamala (great garland), Sumala (fair garland), Bahulochana (many-eyed)."}},{"n":124,"text":"विस्तारो लवणः कूपः कुसुमः सफलोदयः ।\nवृषभो वृषभाङ्काङ्गो मणिबिल्वो जटाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vistara (expanse), Lavana (salt), Kupa (well), Kusuma (flower), Saphalodaya (rising with fruit), Vrishabha (bull), Vrishabhankanga (with the bull sign), Manibilva (jewel-bilva), Jatadhara (matted-haired)."}},{"n":125,"text":"इन्दुर्विसर्गः सुमुखः सुरः सर्वायुधः सहः ।\nनिवेदनः सुधाजातः सुगन्धारो महाधनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indu (moon), Visarga (emission), Sumukha (fair-faced), Sura (god), Sarvayudha (all-weaponed), Saha (patient), Nivedana (offering), Sudhajata (born of nectar), Sugandhara (sweetly scented), Mahadhanu (great bow)."}},{"n":126,"text":"गन्धमाली च भगवानुत्थानः सर्वकर्मणाम् ।\nमन्थानो बहुलो बाहुः सकलः सर्वलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gandhamali (fragrant-garlanded), Bhagavan, Utthana (the rising) of all actions, Manthana (churning), Bahula (abundant), Bahu (arm), Sakala (entire), Sarvalochana (all-eyed)."}},{"n":127,"text":"तरस्ताली करस्ताली ऊर्ध्वसंहननो वहः ।\nछत्रं सुच्छत्रो विख्यातः सर्वलोकाश्रयो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tarastali (palm-clapper), Karastali (hand-clapper), Urdhvasamhanana (upright in build), Vaha (bearer), Chhatra (umbrella), Suchchhatra (fine umbrella), Vikhyata (famed), Sarvalokashraya (refuge of all worlds), Mahan."}},{"n":128,"text":"मुण्डो विरूपो विकृतो दण्डिमुण्डो विकुर्वणः ।\nहर्यक्षः ककुभो वज्री दीप्तजिह्वः सहस्रपात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Munda (shaven), Virupa (deformed), Vikrita (altered), Dandimunda (staff-bearing shaven one), Vikurvana (shape-changer), Haryaksha (tawny-eyed), Kakubha (peak), Vajri (thunderbolt-bearer), Diptajihva (bright-tongued), Sahasrapat (thousand-footed)."}},{"n":129,"text":"सहस्रमूर्धा देवेन्द्रः सर्वदेवमयो गुरुः ।\nसहस्रबाहुः सर्वाङ्गः शरण्यः सर्वलोककृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahasramurdha (thousand-headed), Devendra (lord of gods), Sarvadevamaya (made of all gods), Guru (teacher), Sahasrabahu (thousand-armed), Sarvanga (all-limbed), Sharanya (refuge), Sarvalokakrit (maker of all worlds)."}},{"n":130,"text":"पवित्रं त्रिमधुर्मन्त्रः कनिष्ठः कृष्णपिङ्गलः ।\nब्रह्मदण्डविनिर्माता शतघ्नी शतपाशधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pavitra (pure), Trimadhu (threefold sweet), Mantra, Kanishtha (youngest), Krishnapingala (dark-tawny), Brahmadandavinirmata (maker of Brahma's rod), Shataghni (hundred-slayer), Shatapashadhrik (bearer of a hundred nooses)."}},{"n":131,"text":"पद्मगर्भो महागर्भो ब्रह्मगर्भो जलोद्भवः ।\nगभस्तिर्ब्रह्मकृद्ब्रह्मा ब्रह्मविद्ब्राह्मणो गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Padmagarbha (lotus-womb), Mahagarbha (great-womb), Brahmagarbha (womb of Brahman), Jalodbhava (water-born), Gabhasti (ray), Brahmakrit (maker of Brahman), Brahma, Brahmavit (knower of Brahman), Brahmana (brahmin), Gati (goal)."}},{"n":132,"text":"अनन्तरूपो नैकात्मा तिग्मतेजाः स्वयंभुवः ।\nऊर्ध्वगात्मा पशुपतिर्वातरंहा मनोजवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anantarupa (of endless form), Naikatma (of many selves), Tigmatejas (of sharp power), Svayambhuva (the self-born's), Urdhvagatma (of upward self), Pashupati, Vataramha (swift as wind), Manojava (swift as mind)."}},{"n":133,"text":"चन्दनी पद्ममालाग्र्यः सुरभ्युत्तरणो नरः ।\nकर्णिकारमहास्रग्वी नीलमौलिः पिनाकधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chandani (sandal-smeared), Padmamalagrya (foremost with lotus garland), Surabhyuttarana (rescuer from the sweetly scented), Nara (man), Karnikaramahasragvi (wearing a great karnikara garland), Nilamauli (blue-crowned), Pinakadhrik."}},{"n":134,"text":"उमापतिरुमाकान्तो जाह्नवीधृगुमाधवः ।\nवरो वराहो वरदो वरेशः सुमहास्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Umapati, Umakanta (beloved of Uma), Jahnavidhrik (bearer of the Ganga), Umadhava (husband of Uma), Vara, Varaha (boar), Varada (boon-giver), Varesha (lord of boons), Sumahasvana (of mighty voice)."}},{"n":135,"text":"महाप्रसादो दमनः शत्रुहा श्वेतपिङ्गलः ।\nप्रीतात्मा प्रयतात्मा च संयतात्मा प्रधानधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mahaprasada (great grace), Damana (subduer), Shatruha (foe-slayer), Shvetapingala (white-tawny), Pritatma (pleased soul), Prayatatma (disciplined soul), Samyatatma (controlled soul), Pradhanadhrik (bearer of Pradhana)."}},{"n":136,"text":"सर्वपार्श्वसुतस्तार्क्ष्यो धर्मसाधारणो वरः ।\nचराचरात्मा सूक्ष्मात्मा सुवृषो गोवृषेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvaparshvasuta (son in every side), Tarkshya, Dharmasadharana (common to all dharma), Vara, Characharatma (self of moving and unmoving), Sukshmatma (subtle self), Suvrisha (good bull), Govrisheshvara (lord of the bull and cow)."}},{"n":137,"text":"साध्यर्षिर्वसुरादित्यो विवस्वान्सविता मृडः ।\nव्यासः सर्वस्य संक्षेपो विस्तरः पर्ययो नयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sadhyarshi (sage of the Sadhyas), Vasu, Aditya, Vivasvan, Savita, Mrida (the gracious), Vyasa (arranger), Sarvasya Sankshepa (condensation of all), Vistara (expansion), Paryaya (turn), Naya (method)."}},{"n":138,"text":"ऋतुः संवत्सरो मासः पक्षः संख्यासमापनः ।\nकला काष्ठा लवो मात्रा मुहूर्तोऽहः क्षपाः क्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ritu (season), Samvatsara (year), Masa (month), Paksha (fortnight), Sankhyasamapana (completer of counting), Kala, Kashtha, Lava, Matra, Muhurta, Ahah (day), Kshapa (night), Kshana (moment)."}},{"n":139,"text":"विश्वक्षेत्रं प्रजाबीजं लिङ्गमाद्यस्त्वनिन्दितः ।\nसदसद्व्यक्तमव्यक्तं पिता माता पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishvakshetra (field of the universe), Prajabija (seed of creatures), Linga (sign), Adya (the first), Anindita, Sadasadvyakta (being, non-being, manifest), Avyakta (unmanifest), Pita (father), Mata (mother), Pitamaha (grandfather)."}},{"n":140,"text":"स्वर्गद्वारं प्रजाद्वारं मोक्षद्वारं त्रिविष्टपम् ।\nनिर्वाणं ह्लादनं चैव ब्रह्मलोकः परा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Svargadvara (gate of heaven), Prajadvara (gate of progeny), Mokshadvara (gate of liberation), Trivishtapa (the third heaven), Nirvana (extinction), Hladana (delight), Brahmaloka (Brahma's world), Para Gati (supreme goal)."}},{"n":141,"text":"देवासुरविनिर्माता देवासुरपरायणः ।\nदेवासुरगुरुर्देवो देवासुरनमस्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devasuravinirmata (maker of gods and demons), Devasuraparayana (refuge of gods and demons), Devasuraguru (teacher of gods and demons), Deva, Devasuranamaskrita (saluted by gods and demons)."}},{"n":142,"text":"देवासुरमहामात्रो देवासुरगणाश्रयः ।\nदेवासुरगणाध्यक्षो देवासुरगणाग्रणीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devasuramahamatra (great measure of gods and demons), Devasuraganashraya (refuge of the hosts of gods and demons), Devasuraganadhyaksha (overseer of their hosts), Devasuraganagrani (leader of their hosts)."}},{"n":143,"text":"देवातिदेवो देवर्षिर्देवासुरवरप्रदः ।\nदेवासुरेश्वरो देवो देवासुरमहेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devatideva (god beyond gods), Devarshi (divine sage), Devasuravaraprada (giver of boons to gods and demons), Devasureshvara (lord of gods and demons), Deva, Devasuramaheshvara (great lord of gods and demons)."}},{"n":144,"text":"सर्वदेवमयोऽचिन्त्यो देवतात्मात्मसंभवः ।\nउद्भिदस्त्रिक्रमो वैद्यो विरजो विरजोम्बरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sarvadevamaya (made of all gods), Achintya (unthinkable), Devatatma (soul of the gods), Atmasambhava (self-born), Udbhid (that bursts forth), Trikrama (three-strided), Vaidya (physician), Viraja (free of passion), Virajambara (wearing stainless garments)."}},{"n":145,"text":"ईड्यो हस्ती सुरव्याघ्रो देवसिंहो नरर्षभः ।\nविबुधाग्रवरः श्रेष्ठः सर्वदेवोत्तमोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Idya (worthy of praise), Hasti (elephant), Suravyaghra (tiger of gods), Devasimha (lion of gods), Nararshabha (bull among men), Vibudhagravara (chief of the wise), Shreshtha (best), Sarvadevottamottama (best of the best of all gods)."}},{"n":146,"text":"प्रयुक्तः शोभनो वज्र ईशानः प्रभुरव्ययः ।\nगुरुः कान्तो निजः सर्गः पवित्रः सर्ववाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prayukta (employed), Shobhana (radiant), Vajra (thunderbolt), Ishana (ruler), Prabhu (lord), Avyaya (imperishable), Guru (teacher), Kanta (beloved), Nija (own), Sarga (creation), Pavitra (pure), Sarvavahana (carrying all)."}},{"n":147,"text":"शृङ्गी शृङ्गप्रियो बभ्रू राजराजो निरामयः ।\nअभिरामः सुरगणो विरामः सर्वसाधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shringi (horned), Shringapriya (fond of horns), Babhru (tawny), Rajaraja (king of kings), Niramaya (free of ailment), Abhirama (pleasing), Suragana (host of gods), Virama (rest), Sarvasadhana (means of all)."}},{"n":148,"text":"ललाटाक्षो विश्वदेहो हरिणो ब्रह्मवर्चसः ।\nस्थावराणां पतिश्चैव नियमेन्द्रियवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lalataksha (with an eye on the brow), Vishvadeha (body of the universe), Harina (golden), Brahmavarchasa (radiant with Brahman), Sthavaranam Pati (lord of immovables), Niyamendriyavardhana (strengthener of restraint and senses)."}},{"n":149,"text":"सिद्धार्थः सर्वभूतार्थोऽचिन्त्यः सत्यव्रतः शुचिः ।\nव्रताधिपः परं ब्रह्म मुक्तानां परमा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Siddhartha (fulfilled), Sarvabhutartha (purpose of all beings), Achintya, Satyavrata (true to vows), Shuchi (pure), Vratadhipa (lord of vows), Parama Brahma (supreme Brahman), Muktanam Parama Gati (supreme goal of the freed)."}},{"n":150,"text":"विमुक्तो मुक्ततेजाश्च श्रीमाञ्श्रीवर्धनो जगत् ।\nयथाप्रधानं भगवानिति भक्त्या स्तुतो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vimukta (liberated), Muktatejas (of liberated radiance), Shriman (glorious), Shrivardhana (increaser of prosperity), Jagat (the world). Thus, according to my devotion and as the principal ones, the Lord has been praised by me."}},{"n":151,"text":"यं न ब्रह्मादयो देवा विदुर्यं न महर्षयः ।\nतं स्तव्यमर्च्यं वन्द्यं च कः स्तोष्यति जगत्पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom Brahma and the other gods do not know, and the great sages do not know, who will praise such a Lord of the world, worthy of praise, worship and salutation?"}},{"n":152,"text":"भक्तिमेव पुरस्कृत्य मया यज्ञपतिर्वसुः ।\nततोऽभ्यनुज्ञां प्राप्यैव स्तुतो मतिमतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting devotion first, I have praised him, the Lord of sacrifice, Vasu, best of the wise, only after receiving his permission."}},{"n":153,"text":"शिवमेभिः स्तुवन्देवं नामभिः पुष्टिवर्धनैः ।\nनित्ययुक्तः शुचिर्भूत्वा प्राप्नोत्यात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is ever devoted and pure, praising Shiva with these names that increase well-being, reaches the Self by the Self."}},{"n":154,"text":"एतद्धि परमं ब्रह्म स्वयं गीतं स्वयंभुवा ।\nऋषयश्चैव देवाश्च स्तुवन्त्येतेन तत्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the supreme Brahman, sung by the Self-born himself; sages and gods praise the Supreme with it."}},{"n":155,"text":"स्तूयमानो महादेवः प्रीयते चात्मनामभिः ।\nभक्तानुकम्पी भगवानात्मसंस्थान्करोति तान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When praised with the names of his own self, Mahadeva is pleased; the compassionate Lord establishes his devotees in the Self."}},{"n":156,"text":"तथैव च मनुष्येषु ये मनुष्याः प्रधानतः ।\nआस्तिकाः श्रद्दधानाश्च बहुभिर्जन्मभिः स्तवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, among men, those who are foremost believers and faithful, who after many births praise him with hymns."}},{"n":157,"text":"जाग्रतश्च स्वपन्तश्च व्रजन्तः पथि संस्थिताः ।\nस्तुवन्ति स्तूयमानाश्च तुष्यन्ति च रमन्ति च ।\nजन्मकोटिसहस्रेषु नानासंसारयोनिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether waking or sleeping, walking or standing on the road, they praise and are praised, are satisfied and rejoice, through thousands of crores of births in various cycles of existence."}},{"n":158,"text":"जन्तोर्विशुद्धपापस्य भवे भक्तिः प्रजायते ।\nउत्पन्ना च भवे भक्तिरनन्या सर्वभावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a creature whose sin is purified, devotion to Bhava arises; and once arisen, that devotion becomes exclusive and total."}},{"n":159,"text":"कारणं भावितं तस्य सर्वमुक्तस्य सर्वतः ।\nएतद्देवेषु दुष्प्रापं मनुष्येषु न लभ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is a cause well established in one who is wholly freed on every side. This is hard to get even for gods, and men do not obtain it."}},{"n":160,"text":"निर्विघ्ना निश्चला रुद्रे भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी ।\nतस्यैव च प्रसादेन भक्तिरुत्पद्यते नृणाम् ।\nयया यान्ति परां सिद्धिं तद्भावगतचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devotion to Rudra, unobstructed, unshaken and unwavering, arises in men only by his grace; through it, those whose minds are fixed on him reach supreme success."}},{"n":161,"text":"ये सर्वभावोपगताः परत्वेनाभवन्नराः ।\nप्रपन्नवत्सलो देवः संसारात्तान्समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men who come to him with their whole being and hold him as supreme, the God who loves those who take refuge lifts out of the cycle of rebirth."}},{"n":162,"text":"एवमन्ये न कुर्वन्ति देवाः संसारमोचनम् ।\nमनुष्याणां महादेवादन्यत्रापि तपोबलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other gods give men release from the cycle, other than Mahadeva, even through the strength of austerity elsewhere."}},{"n":163,"text":"इति तेनेन्द्रकल्पेन भगवान्सदसत्पतिः ।\nकृत्तिवासाः स्तुतः कृष्ण तण्डिना शुद्धबुद्धिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, Krishna, the Blessed One, lord of being and non-being, the one clad in an elephant hide, was praised by the pure-minded Tandi, who was like Indra."}},{"n":164,"text":"स्तवमेतं भगवतो ब्रह्मा स्वयमधारयत् ।\nब्रह्मा प्रोवाच शक्राय शक्रः प्रोवाच मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma himself held this hymn of the Lord. Brahma told it to Indra, and Indra told it to Death."}},{"n":165,"text":"मृत्युः प्रोवाच रुद्राणां रुद्रेभ्यस्तण्डिमागमत् ।\nमहता तपसा प्राप्तस्तण्डिना ब्रह्मसद्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death told it to the Rudras, and from the Rudras it came to Tandi, who obtained it in Brahma's abode through great austerity."}},{"n":166,"text":"तण्डिः प्रोवाच शुक्राय गौतमायाह भार्गवः ।\nवैवस्वताय मनवे गौतमः प्राह माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tandi told it to Shukra; Bhargava told Gautama; Gautama, Madhava, told it to Manu Vaivasvata."}},{"n":167,"text":"नारायणाय साध्याय मनुरिष्टाय धीमते ।\nयमाय प्राह भगवान्साध्यो नारायणोऽच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Manu told it to Narayana Sadhya, the wise and beloved; the blessed Sadhya Narayana, Acyuta, told it to Yama."}},{"n":168,"text":"नाचिकेताय भगवानाह वैवस्वतो यमः ।\nमार्कण्डेयाय वार्ष्णेय नाचिकेतोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed Yama Vaivasvata told it to Nachiketa; Nachiketa, descendant of Vrishni, told it to Markandeya."}},{"n":169,"text":"मार्कण्डेयान्मया प्राप्तं नियमेन जनार्दन ।\nतवाप्यहममित्रघ्न स्तवं दद्म्यद्य विश्रुतम् ।\nस्वर्ग्यमारोग्यमायुष्यं धन्यं बल्यं तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I received it from Markandeya with proper discipline, Janardana, and today, destroyer of foes, I give to you too this renowned hymn, which brings heaven, health, long life, prosperity and strength."}},{"n":170,"text":"न तस्य विघ्नं कुर्वन्ति दानवा यक्षराक्षसाः ।\nपिशाचा यातुधानाश्च गुह्यका भुजगा अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Demons, yakshas, rakshasas, pishachas, yatudhanas, guhyakas and even serpents place no obstacle before him."}},{"n":171,"text":"यः पठेत शुचिर्भूत्वा ब्रह्मचारी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nअभग्नयोगो वर्षं तु सोऽश्वमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, pure, celibate and self-controlled, recites it for a year without breaking the discipline gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}}]}]}